        {
          "title": "Learner workspace contract (AGENTS.md: ask one bounded prediction, wait for the attempt)",
          "clause": "Teaching"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c.recap",
      "kind": "rule",
      "text": "A case label only marks where execution enters a switch; it never ends a case. In this program, the break on line 12 is what ends the switch.",
      "justification": "Entry: 6.8.4.2p5 (control jumps to the statement after the matched label). Labels do not alter control flow: 6.8.1p4. The break on line 12 of programs/fallthrough.c ends the switch: 6.8.6.3p2. The sentence does not claim break is the only way out (return, goto and others also leave); it names what ends this switch.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "ISO/IEC 9899:2018 (C17), working draft N2176",
          "url": "https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n2176.pdf",
          "clause": "§6.8.4.2 ¶5, §6.8.1 ¶4, §6.8.6.3 ¶2"
        }
      ]
    }
